   {
    "_comment": "FROZEN ID, dead fiction (spec 7 amendment 1): the display name was 'A Second Door'. The entity id is shipped and frozen; the fiction is not. This is a sealed rune-door full of wardwork by the hand that cut the inn's frame -- never a second Magical Door, never another portal. No QA script pins the old label.",
    "_comment_door": "Act V beat 3, the FIGHT path. door_when is checked BEFORE the interact arm (interactions.gd prop branch order), so once seal_opened banks this stops being a thing to read and becomes a way through. seal_opened banks ONLY on Pisces' open-it fork, so the TALK and SKILL paths leave this door shut forever, as #270 requires.",
    "_comment_reading": "Act V beat 2, THE READING (#270). Three eyes on one door, the pantry-door consolidation idiom. LATER-SATISFIED-WINS across `variants` makes the bare interact a two-stage narration: with the descent agreed Pisces matches the hand (read_the_seal_runes), and his next read names the appetite (read_the_feeding_ward). That staging is load-bearing -- no main-line beat may sit behind a Skill the player's build might not own (spec 6) -- so the escort is the guaranteed producer of both reads. Pre-descent arms bank `sensed_something_deeper`, never the real reads, which ORDER-GATES the quest: nothing in Act V can bank from a curious Act IV visit.",
