   {
    "_comment": "Act V: THE SEAL'S WARDEN. present_when is validator-forbidden on encounters, so it stands here from first arrival, VISIBLE AND INERT (the rift_vermin_leak pattern) with its own observe + gate_closed_toast. encounter_when arms it on seal_opened alone, which only the FIGHT fork banks. trigger_radius 1 makes it UNSKIPPABLE on that fork -- (18,7) is the only walkable approach to the door and sits one cell off; a sneaking player still slips by and banks sneaked_past_danger. CELL (19,6) is reachable only from (19,5), so it blocks no route, and it is NOT (18,7), which delve_fight stands on. Roster: `seal_warden`, a distinct id per combatants.json:401.",
    "_comment_loot": "DELIBERATELY no `loot` array: every enchanted accessory this fight could plausibly drop (warded_coil_charm, construct_core_shard, guardian_ward_fragment) is a chance-1.0 drop from a fight the player must already have won to be standing here, and `pickup` no-ops a duplicate id. The reward is the room behind it (seal_anchor_rune) plus the quest's resolution_paths grant.",
    "_comment_victory": "on_victory is the ENGINE DEFAULT spelled out (test_combat_data requires the key on every encounter): the warden banks no story counter. Act V's resolution belongs to the room behind it -- vault_anchor_stone's open banks seal_resolved -- so sneaking past and flattening it reach the same beat at different cost.",
